th and without a dispensing technician</article-title><source>Int J Pharm Pract</source><year>1995</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Savage I. Time for customer contact in pharmacies with and without a dispensing technician. Int J Pharm Pract 1995;3:193&#x02013;9. </citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Emmerton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Becket</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilbanks</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Application of electronic work sampling technology in New Zealand community pharmacy</article-title><source>J Soc Adm Pharm</source><year>1998</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>191</fpage><lpage>5</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Emmerton L, Becket G, Gilbanks L. Application of electronic work sampling technology in New Zealand community pharmacy. J Soc Adm Pharm 1998;15:191&#x02013;5. </citation></ref><ref id="CR21"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rutter</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunt</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Darracott</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Subjective evaluation of how community pharmacists in Great Britain spend their time</article-title><source>J Soc Adm Pharm</source><year>1998</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>252</fpage><lpage>61</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rutter P, Hunt A, Darracott R, Jones I. Subjective evaluation of how community pharmacists in Great Britain spend their time. J Soc Adm Pharm 1998;15:252&#x02013;61. </citation></ref><ref id="CR22"